---@class cloudflare.magic_transit.GreTunnelsBulkUpdateResponseModifiedGreTunnelsItem
---@field id string Identifier
---@field cloudflare_gre_endpoint string The IP address assigned to the Cloudflare side of the GRE tunnel.
---@field customer_gre_endpoint string The IP address assigned to the customer side of the GRE tunnel.
---@field interface_address string A 31-bit prefix (/31 in CIDR notation) supporting two hosts, one for each side of the tunnel. Select the subnet from the following private IP space: 10.0.0.0–10.255.255.255, 172.16.0.0–172.31.255.255, 192.168.0.0–192.168.255.255.
---@field name string The name of the tunnel. The name cannot contain spaces or special characters, must be 15 characters or less, and cannot share a name with another GRE tunnel.
---@field automatic_return_routing? boolean|distilled.Null True if automatic stateful return routing should be enabled for a tunnel, false otherwise. Requires the `coupler_integration` account flag to be enabled; requests setting this to `true` without that flag will be rejected.
---@field bgp? cloudflare.magic_transit.GreTunnelsBulkUpdateResponseModifiedGreTunnelsItemBgp|distilled.Null
---@field bgp_status? cloudflare.magic_transit.GreTunnelsBulkUpdateResponseModifiedGreTunnelsItemBgpStatus|distilled.Null
---@field created_on? string|distilled.Null The date and time the tunnel was created.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null An optional description of the GRE tunnel.
---@field health_check? cloudflare.magic_transit.GreTunnelsBulkUpdateResponseModifiedGreTunnelsItemHealthCheck|distilled.Null
---@field interface_address6? string|distilled.Null A 127 bit IPV6 prefix from within the virtual_subnet6 prefix space with the address being the first IP of the subnet and not same as the address of virtual_subnet6. Eg if virtual_subnet6 is 2606:54c1:7:0:a9fe:12d2::/127 , interface_address6 could be 2606:54c1:7:0:a9fe:12d2:1:200/127
---@field modified_on? string|distilled.Null The date and time the tunnel was last modified.
---@field mtu? number|distilled.Null Maximum Transmission Unit (MTU) in bytes for the GRE tunnel. The minimum value is 576.
---@field ttl? number|distilled.Null Time To Live (TTL) in number of hops of the GRE tunnel.

---@class cloudflare.magic_transit.GreTunnelsBulkUpdateResponseModifiedGreTunnelsItemBgp
---@field customer_asn number ASN used on the customer end of the BGP session
---@field export_filter_id? string|distilled.Null ID of the BGP filter profile applied to routes advertised to the customer.
---@field extra_prefixes? cloudflare.magic_transit.GreTunnelsBulkUpdateResponseModifiedGreTunnelsItemBgpExtraPrefixesList|distilled.Null Prefixes in this list will be advertised to the customer device, in addition to the routes in the Magic routing table. Each entry must be a network address in CIDR notation with no host bits set (for example `192.0.2.0/24`, not `192.0.2.1/24`) and must not repeat another entry. IPv6 prefixes are accepted only when the tunnel has an `interface_address6`.
---@field import_filter_id? string|distilled.Null ID of the BGP filter profile applied to routes received from the customer.
---@field md5_key? string|distilled.Null MD5 key to use for session authentication.

