---@field interface_address string A 31-bit prefix (/31 in CIDR notation) supporting two hosts, one for each side of the tunnel. Select the subnet from the following private IP space: 10.0.0.0–10.255.255.255, 172.16.0.0–172.31.255.255, 192.168.0.0–192.168.255.255.
---@field name string The name of the IPsec tunnel. The name cannot share a name with other tunnels.
---@field allow_null_cipher? boolean|distilled.Null When `true`, the tunnel can use a null-cipher (`ENCR_NULL`) in the ESP tunnel (Phase 2).
---@field automatic_return_routing? boolean|distilled.Null True if automatic stateful return routing should be enabled for a tunnel, false otherwise. Requires the `coupler_integration` account flag to be enabled; requests setting this to `true` without that flag will be rejected.
---@field bgp? cloudflare.magic_transit.IpsecTunnelsUpdateResponseModifiedIpsecTunnelBgp|distilled.Null
---@field bgp_status? cloudflare.magic_transit.IpsecTunnelsUpdateResponseModifiedIpsecTunnelBgpStatus|distilled.Null
---@field created_on? string|distilled.Null The date and time the tunnel was created.
---@field custom_remote_identities? cloudflare.magic_transit.IpsecTunnelsUpdateResponseModifiedIpsecTunnelCustomRemoteIdentities|distilled.Null
---@field customer_endpoint? string|distilled.Null The IP address assigned to the customer side of the IPsec tunnel. Not required, but must be set for proactive traceroutes to work.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null An optional description forthe IPsec tunnel.
---@field health_check? cloudflare.magic_transit.IpsecTunnelsUpdateResponseModifiedIpsecTunnelHealthCheck|distilled.Null
---@field interface_address6? string|distilled.Null A 127 bit IPV6 prefix from within the virtual_subnet6 prefix space with the address being the first IP of the subnet and not same as the address of virtual_subnet6. Eg if virtual_subnet6 is 2606:54c1:7:0:a9fe:12d2::/127 , interface_address6 could be 2606:54c1:7:0:a9fe:12d2:1:200/127
---@field modified_on? string|distilled.Null The date and time the tunnel was last modified.
---@field psk_metadata? cloudflare.magic_transit.IpsecTunnelsUpdateResponseModifiedIpsecTunnelPskMetadata|distilled.Null The PSK metadata that includes when the PSK was generated.
---@field replay_protection? boolean|distilled.Null If `true`, then IPsec replay protection will be supported in the Cloudflare-to-customer direction.

---@class cloudflare.magic_transit.IpsecTunnelsUpdateResponseModifiedIpsecTunnelBgp
